       }
      ],
      "text": "**Yes.** As of **4 p.m. Saturday, October 17, Singapore time**, the 24-hour PSI was **132–191 across Singapore—all in the Unhealthy range**. The more immediate 1-hour PM₂.₅ reading was **High** in the west, central, south and east; it reached **221 µg/m³ in the west**. ([channelnewsasia.com](https://www.channelnewsasia.com/singapore/singapore-haze-psi-pm25-oct-17-6466816))\n\nIf you’re heading out, **avoid strenuous outdoor exercise for now**. Singapore’s Ministry of Health advises older people, pregnant people, and those with chronic heart or lung conditions to avoid outdoor activity when the hourly PM₂.₅ reading is High. Conditions can change by the hour, so check the **1-hour PM₂.₅ reading** for your area before going out. ([moh.gov.sg](https://www.moh.gov.sg/others/haze/))",
      "type": "output_text",
